From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:14:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] gl-renderer: log once instead of aborting when YUV uniforms are missing

On the Raspberry Pi 4 (v3d, Mesa 26.2) an NV12 SAND128 buffer imported
as separate Y and UV planes is drawn with the Y_UV shader variant, and
the compiled shader comes back without the yuv_coefficients/yuv_offsets
uniforms. gl_shader_load_config_representation() asserts that only the
EXTERNAL and RGBA variants may lack them, so weston died with SIGABRT,
which took down the qemu display connection and with it the AAOS guest
(DomA).

Replace the assert with a one-time weston_log() that names the variant,
and return without loading the uniforms, as the allowed variants already
do.

This is the weston 16.0.0 version. 16.0.0 contains upstream commit
5c49563ef49a ("gl-shaders: Remove asserts relying on shader compiler
behavior") and allows the RGBA variant as well, but still asserts for
Y_UV, so the change is still needed; RGBA stays an accepted variant
here.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [workaround for v3d dropping the uniforms; replaces an upstream assert]
---
--- a/libweston/renderer-gl/gl-shaders.c
+++ b/libweston/renderer-gl/gl-shaders.c
@@ -825,8 +825,17 @@
 
 	if (shader->yuv_coefficients_uniform == -1 ||
 	    shader->yuv_offsets_uniform == -1) {
-		assert(shader->key.variant == SHADER_VARIANT_EXTERNAL ||
-		       shader->key.variant == SHADER_VARIANT_RGBA);
+		/*
+		 * The v3d compiler drops these uniforms for the
+		 * Y_UV variant of an NV12 SAND128 buffer too; the assert aborted weston.
+		 */
+		static bool logged;
+		if (shader->key.variant != SHADER_VARIANT_EXTERNAL &&
+		    shader->key.variant != SHADER_VARIANT_RGBA && !logged) {
+			logged = true;
+			weston_log("gl-renderer: YUV uniforms missing for variant %d\n",
+				   shader->key.variant);
+		}
 		return;
 	}
 
